# q4-48k — RECOMMENDED profile: 48K context, q4 (nvfp4-layout) main KV.
#
# This is byte-for-byte the flag set of the measured production boot
# (2026-10-23 20:07 PDT, image m31-flash-exl3-spark:dev-fdd7736-41fdb7d with
# the plugin at the pinned rev, MIMALLOC_PURGE_DELAY=0 +
# MIMALLOC_RESET_DELAY=0 as serve.sh passes them). Every value here is a
# measured number; nothing is derived. See README "Measured results" for what
# this profile produced and "Profiles" for the other profiles.
#
# Main KV pool: q4 (576 B/token/layer via the plugin's VLLM_EXL3_Q4KV
# reroute); the MSA indexer key cache and the DSpark draft pool stay fp8.
# KVB is the measured pool budget and equals scripts/kvb.py's q4 budget for
# 49152 tokens (46.25 KiB/token + 2% margin); the engine allocated 50,048
# tokens of KV at this budget (1.02x the context limit).
#
# 48K is only servable together with the mimalloc purge/reset delays this
# repo defaults to 0: without them the first request after boot was
# guard-killed at 48K (ready MemAvailable 0.32 GiB). See README "Known
# limits". q4-32k is the same flags at 32K with ~0.8 GiB more headroom.
MAXLEN="${MAXLEN:-49152}"
KV_Q4="${KV_Q4:-1}"
KVB="${KVB:-2374395495}"
KV_CACHE_DTYPE="${KV_CACHE_DTYPE:-fp8}"          # env.sh's q4 gate flips this to nvfp4
INDEXER_KV_DTYPE="${INDEXER_KV_DTYPE:-fp8}"
INDEXER_MXFP8="${INDEXER_MXFP8:-1}"
# Chunked prefill + CUDA graphs + compile mode (measured).
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS="${MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS:-1024}"
CG_MODE="${CG_MODE:-FULL_DECODE_ONLY}"
CAPTURE_SIZES="${CAPTURE_SIZES:-1,2,3,4}"
COMPILE_MODE="${COMPILE_MODE:-0}"
MALLOC_ARENA_MAX="${MALLOC_ARENA_MAX:-2}"
# DSpark draft k=3, fp8 draft KV on the Triton attention backend (the only
# fp8-draft pair that boots on GB10; required by the q4 gate).
DSPARK="${DSPARK:-1}"
DSPARK_NUM_SPEC="${DSPARK_NUM_SPEC:-3}"
DSPARK_ATTN_BACKEND="${DSPARK_ATTN_BACKEND:-TRITON_ATTN}"
DSPARK_KV_DTYPE="${DSPARK_KV_DTYPE:-fp8}"
DSPARK_DRAFT_SAMPLE="${DSPARK_DRAFT_SAMPLE:-probabilistic}"
DSPARK_REJECTION="${DSPARK_REJECTION:-block}"
# Boot-time FlashInfer autotune off (measured: more free memory at ready,
# same ms/step; the warm-up request pays the JIT-compile cost instead).
FLASHINFER_AUTOTUNE="${FLASHINFER_AUTOTUNE:-0}"
# UMA load hygiene (all measured, see scripts/env.sh).
LOAD_TRIM="${LOAD_TRIM:-1}"
EMBED_ALIAS="${EMBED_ALIAS:-1}"
DRAFT_VOCAB_META="${DRAFT_VOCAB_META:-1}"
TRIM_BEFORE_KV="${TRIM_BEFORE_KV:-1}"
MOE_TEMP_ROWS="${MOE_TEMP_ROWS:-512}"
PERIODIC_TRIM_S="${PERIODIC_TRIM_S:-30}"
JIT_WARMUP_THREADS="${JIT_WARMUP_THREADS:-1}"
COMPILE_THREADS="${COMPILE_THREADS:-1}"
# Warm-up: the standalone serve waits for /v1/models and pays the first
# JIT-compile cost in a logged request before printing READY.
SERVE_WAIT="${SERVE_WAIT:-1}"
WARMUP="${WARMUP:-1}"
# Guard floor: 0.2 GiB, the value the measured boot ran. REQUIRED, not a
# suggestion: the first request after boot costs a MAXLEN-independent
# ~0.33 GiB host-memory transient (plus ~0.18 GiB more at the first ~8K
# prefill) that malloc_trim recovers only ~30 s later, and this profile's
# measured ready MemAvailable is 1.28 GiB with a 733-779 MiB lowest guard
# sample across two boots — at the public default 0.5 GiB floor the
# transient would trip the guard during the warm-up. The warm-up request
# absorbs the transient BEFORE the READY line; do not lower this further.
GUARD_MEM_FLOOR_KIB="${GUARD_MEM_FLOOR_KIB:-209716}"